  "summary": "In September 1928, on returning from holiday to his laboratory at St Mary's Hospital, London, Alexander Fleming found a staphylococcus culture contaminated by mould with a bacteria-free ring around it. He identified the mould as Penicillium notatum and named its antibacterial product penicillin. He shared the 1945 Nobel Prize for the discovery.",
